    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0060" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg6"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President
                        Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d7-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-05-28">May 28, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>685. Prime Minister to President Roosevelt top secret and personal.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Cabinet and I are most grateful to you for your number 543<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d7-f2"/> about my 680.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d7-f3"/></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I still think that a short visit is, above all things, desirable for the
                        Staffs and above all for you, but any time after D + 14 might be convenient
                        to you, and would be received with rejoicing by us. I am delighted at what
                        you say and that you are keeping this in view. Doctor Churchill informs you
                        that a sea voyage in one of your great new battleships would do you no end
                        of good.</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d7-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d7-f1-content">
                <p>Channel of transmission to Washington not indicated; forwarded by the White House
                    Map Room to Roosevelt, who was then at Shangri La (a mountain camp in Maryland),
                    as telegram No. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Red</hi> 40.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d7-f2" n="2" xml:id="d7-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d7-f3" n="3" xml:id="d7-f3-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg5">p. 5</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
